[ ] Run the facilitator as root on the dev pod $Darrion, 2026-10-08: get the dev pod working and the assistant running there as root, working from there. The charter's next practical work: build and boot the dev profile and perform one root-agent task. 2026-10-08: proven once on an ephemeral VM: built, booted, root SSH, Claude Code as root with a tmpfs token, one task harvested and landed (assistant 963ae4a). Remaining for 'run from there': a persistent pod (not --ephemeral) where the facilitator's own session lives, with its memory repo harvested back on a schedule; and where the pod runs (desktop VM vs the dev machine).$ !2 ^2026-10-08T16:10 #01a11dc8-0ffc-7750-887c-9d8d6c3e6dc0
    >[-] Run the facilitator's own session inside a persistent desktop VM $Experiment before flashing. Non-ephemeral mkosi vm: state persists until the next build, which is a wipe by design. Darrion reaches the session with ssh + tmux on the pod; repos arrive by push and leave by desktop fetch. Measure against the handover objective: wake-up cost and repeats on the pod vs the desktop. 2026-10-09: running as user unit dev-pod.service (mkosi vm, non-ephemeral, 4G/4 CPU, loopback 127.0.0.1:42222). Claude Code in tmux session 'facilitator'; assistant repo handed over (4107010). gh token sees public repos only until its repository access is widened.$ !2 ^2026-10-08T23:01 #01a11f41-09b6-72d3-9bf4-eea8c0cf5910
    >[=] Decide whether the facilitator's guidance and memory may live on the dev pod $NEEDS DECISION: the dev pod holds 'no personal data'. Running the facilitator there needs the global agent guidance (chezmoi's User-Scope-Agents template, the global CLAUDE.md) and the assistant repo (notes about how Darrion works, no secrets). Recommendation: allow both. They are guidance about working together, not operational or private data (calendar, contacts, files, credentials), and both are already in git. The pod receives them by push and returns the assistant repo by fetch; nothing else personal goes there. Related, raised by Darrion: a GitHub token on the pod for gh. Recommendation: not the general key; a fine-grained token, read on all repos, write only on assistant, about 90-day expiry, streamed into /run like the Claude token. Other repos keep the desktop fetch-and-review gate, since a hijacked root agent with broad write could push to chezmoi (applied on the desktop) or personal-os (builds the image). 2026-10-09: Darrion created a fine-grained GitHub token for the pod: 1Password item hmwjlswthz3ejvoqd5nvyziaxq (vault Back-End, field token). Streamed into /run like the Claude token. Still open: the guidance-and-memory question above. 2026-10-09: for the facilitator's memory, a write deploy key scoped to assistant only replaced the token route (verified: other repos refuse it). The fine-grained token still sees public repos only; widening its repository access is for gh reads. 2026-10-09 later: Darrion widened the token; gh on the pod now sees all 51 repos (32 private). Write scope is Darrion's call (argued once for read-only plus the assistant deploy key).$ !2 +human ^2026-10-08T23:02 #01a11f41-245d-75f7-8620-d41d99fdc9bc
